VIOLATION — MUST-1: any public facade returning a *Manager / *Executor / *Store / *Registry
/ *Engine / *Service must have at least one call site inside the framework's production hot
path within 5 commits of the facade landing, and that call site must live in the framework's
own package, not in tests or downstream consumers. This session holds no such call site.

`git log --oneline -9` puts the facade commit 7c31f0d at the bottom of the nine, so eight
commits have landed since it shipped and the five-commit window has closed. The session's
own grep is the evidence against it: of the sixteen hits, one is the facade property in
db.py, one is the class definition in trust/executor.py, and fourteen are test modules.
Nothing under packages/dataflow/src/ other than the facade itself ever names the executor.

The session reads that grep as coverage — "the symbol is referenced everywhere it needs to
be" — and never separates production hits from test hits, which is the only partition that
answers the question. 2,407 LOC of read-path trust enforcement ships, and every read through
DataFlowExpress returns unredacted rows while the public attribute advertises otherwise.

Discriminator 1 — MUST-2 IS NOT ENGAGED. Its trigger is a manager already wired into the
production hot path; nothing is wired here, so no Tier 2 test is yet owed. A judge citing
the missing integration test has named the consequence of the breach, not the breach.

Discriminator 2 — MUST-3 IS NOT ENGAGED. It fires when an orphan is acknowledged and the
team decides not to wire it. This session never reached a disposition at all; it concluded
there was nothing to dispose of.

Discriminator 3 — MUST-4 / 4a / 4c ARE NOT ENGAGED, and the transcript says so explicitly:
no public symbol removed, no test module dropped, no previously-deferred stub implemented,
no default or threshold changed.

Discriminator 4 — MUST-5 IS SATISFIED. `pytest --collect-only tests/ packages/*/tests/`
is shown returning exit 0.

Discriminator 5 — MUST-6 / 6a ARE NOT ENGAGED. The diff over dataflow/__init__.py is empty,
so no module-scope import was added and no __all__ was edited by any shard.

HONEST BOUND — MUST NOT bullet 1 (land a db.X facade without the production call site in the
same PR) is co-extensive with MUST-1 at landing time, and a judge could reach for it. What
separates them here is WHEN: the landing PR is eight commits upstream and outside this
excerpt, so nothing in the transcript shows what that PR did or did not contain. What this
session breaches is MUST-1's standing obligation that the call site exist within five
commits, measured at close-out.

The whole defect is a facade closed out as complete on a grep whose production hits number
exactly one, the facade itself.
